read from top to bottom. $B[r][c] = A[c][N-1-r]$. This matches the logic.\n    *   **Bottom-Right (BR):** This corresponds to the input grid rotated 180 degrees (Rot 180).\n        *   Verification (Pair 2): BR Row 0 is `9 9 3 0 0 8`. Input Row 5 (last row) is `8 0 0 3 9 9`. Rot 180 reverses the order of elements in the last row. $B[r][c] = A[N-1-r][N-1-c]$. This matches.\n\n**Implementation Plan:**\n1.  Read the input grid size $N$.\n2.  Define helper functions or logic to compute the four rotated versions of the grid: `rot90cw`, `rot270`, `rot180`.\n3.  Construct the output grid of size $2N \\times 2N$ by stitching these quadrants together.\n\n**Verification of Rotation Logic:**\n*   **Rot 90 CW:** `new[r][c] = grid[N-1-c][r]` (mapping the first column to the first row in bottom-to-top order).\n*   **Rot 270 (CCW):** `new[r][c] = grid[c][N-1-r]` (mapping the last column to the first row in top-to-bottom order).\n*   **Rot 180:** `new[r][c] = grid[N-1-r][N-1-c]`.\n\nThe test input is a 14x14 grid. The code will handle any square grid size $N$.\n\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    \n    # Helper to create Rot 90 CW\n    # Formula: B[r][c] = A[N-1-c][r]\n    def rot90cw(g):\n        return [[g[n - 1 - c][r] for c in range(n)] for r in range(n)]\n    \n    # Helper to create Rot 270 (90 CCW)\n    # Formula: B[r][c] = A[c][N-1-r]\n    def rot270(g):\n        return [[g[c][n - 1 - r] for c in range(n)] for r in range(n)]\n    \n    # Helper to create Rot 180\n    # Formula: B[r][c] = A[N-1-r][N-1-c]\n    def rot180(g):\n        return [[g[n - 1 - r][n - 1 - c] for c in range(n)] for r in range(n)]\n    \n    # Calculate quadrants\n    tr = rot90cw(grid)\n    bl = rot270(grid)\n    br = rot180(grid)\n    \n    # Stitch quadrants into 2N x 2N output\n    res = [[0] * (2 * n) for _ in range(2 * n)]\n    \n    for r in range(n):\n        for c in range(n):\n            # Top-Left: Input\n            res[r][c] = grid[r][c]\n            # Top-Right: Rot 90 CW\n            res[r][n + c] = tr[r][c]\n            # Bottom-Left: Rot 270 (CCW)\n            res[n + r][c] = bl[r][c]\n            # Bottom-Right: Rot 180\n            res[n + r][n + c] = br[r][c]\n            \n    return res\n```\n\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":true}}]}